<div class="bio">
<h2 id="bio-h">A short version.</h2>
<p class="big">I'm an occupational therapist based in {{ site.baseTown }}. I've spent over six years in pediatric OT, most of it in early-support work with babies and toddlers — birth to three — and their families, using a parent coaching model.</p>
<p>Before my master's in occupational therapy at the {{ site.alumniOf }}, I spent another six years in behavioral medicine at Seattle Children's Hospital, as a mental health counselor and pediatric behavioral specialist on the inpatient unit. That work still shapes how I understand children, families, and behavior today — particularly the habit of asking what a behavior is <em>for</em> before asking how to stop it.</p>
<p>I've worked with children across a wide range of neurodevelopmental, genetic, and medical profiles, in homes, clinics, and developmental preschool classrooms.</p>
<p>I live in {{ site.baseTown }} with my husband, our son, two dogs, and eleven chickens.</p>

